# Every text file keeps LF in the working tree, on every platform. Git's
# default on Windows is `core.autocrlf=true`, and a CRLF working tree breaks
# this repository twice over: a shell script run through `sh` fails on its own
# shebang, and the suite — which writes a file, lets git check it back out, and
# compares the bytes — reads a line ending it never wrote. Measured 2026-09-21
# on a GitHub windows-latest runner: 21 tests failed, every one of them `\r\n`
# against `\n`, from a sealed attempt's file to the generated command manual.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named for the reason, not just covered by the rule above: `install.sh` and
# every husky hook, including the pre-commit gate, stop working on a machine
# whose only fault was cloning with the default configuration.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf

# Binary, so no end-of-line conversion is ever attempted.
*.png binary
